:: StoryTitle
The Price of Prestige

:: StoryData
{"ifid":"B93175A9-0E76-43A8-9832-B1308B8BBE15","format":"Harlowe","format-version":"3.3.9","start":"Intro","zoom":0.6}

:: Intro [intro] {"position":"500,50","size":"100,100"}
(set: $first to "none", $documented to false, $repair to "none", $credit to "none", $challenged to false, $supported to false, $consent to false, $exitAccount to false)
<div class="eyebrow">CMPT 376W / GROUP 15 / AN INTERACTIVE CASE STUDY</div>
<h1>The Price<br>of Prestige</h1>
<p class="deck">A brilliant lab. A hostile workplace.<br>What are you willing to carry?</p>
<p>You are Diane, a new graduate in augmented reality research. Make four major decisions about professional power, technical responsibility, and earned credit. Earlier choices change later conversations and consequences.</p>
<div class="instructions"><strong>How to play</strong><br>Read each scene and select one choice. Use Tab and Enter to navigate by keyboard. Scroll when needed. There is no timer or moral score. Each ending offers a fresh restart. Allow about 10 minutes per route.</div>
<div class="colour-key"><strong>Reading the colours</strong><br><span class="key-support">Green: support or protection</span> <span class="key-caution">Amber: uncertain tradeoffs</span> <span class="key-risk">Red: heightened risk or continuing harm</span><br>These cues highlight pressures, not guaranteed results. Every ending still has costs to consider.</div>
<p class="small">Contains workplace humiliation and retaliation. You may close the game at any time.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Begin Diane's first week->Offer]]</div>
<div class="credits"><strong>Based on ACM's <a href="https://www.acm.org/code-of-ethics/case-studies/abusive-workplace-behavior" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Abusive Workplace Behavior</a></strong><br>Original adaptation dialogue and fictional reporting process.<br><br><strong>Kazi Boni Amin</strong> - programmer and art designer<br><strong>Krrish Setia</strong> - main writer<br><strong>Andy Wang</strong> - editor and secondary writer</div>

:: Offer [scene] {"position":"500,200"}
<div class="eyebrow">ARRIVAL / THE OPPORTUNITY</div>
<h1>A name on the door</h1>
<p>The offer arrived after two interviews and a final exam. Now your badge opens the lab where Max built the AR tracking system you cited in your capstone. Your first salary covers rent without another evening shift.</p>
<p>Through a headset, a wireframe bridge holds steady over the empty conference table. Your assignment is to test how that image moves when the wearer turns.</p>
<blockquote><b>Max</b>"A convincing demo buys us another year. I need people who can keep up."</blockquote>
<p>Eli slides a chair toward you. His test notes are meticulous, but he closes the team chat when Max walks past.</p>
<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"Ask me about the tracker. It's easier when someone shows you the assumptions."</blockquote>
<div class="choices">[[Join the next lab review->Outburst]]</div>

:: Outburst [decision stage-first tone-risk] {"position":"500,350"}
<div class="eyebrow">01 / THE FIRST OUTBURST</div>
<h1>More than criticism</h1>
<p>In your second week, you reverse two labels on a calibration chart. The measurements are intact; the labels need correcting.</p>
<blockquote><b>Max</b>"Did they give you a degree for guessing? I'm not running a remedial class."</blockquote>
<p>He keeps going after you explain the fix. Nobody speaks. The room feels smaller than it did a minute ago.</p>
<p>You want feedback that makes the work better. You also need this job. Jean, the research manager overseeing the lab, could intervene. Before the next milestone, you choose one immediate response.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Ask Jean to intervene->Jean]]
[[Write a factual record while it is fresh->Record]]
[[Stay quiet for now and protect my position->Quiet]]</div>

:: Jean [consequence tone-risk] {"position":"200,500"}
(set: $first to "jean")
<div class="eyebrow">01 / SEEKING SUPPORT</div>
<h1>The manager's calculation</h1>
<blockquote><b>Diane</b>"I can correct the chart. Being insulted in front of everyone makes it harder to ask the next question."</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>Jean</b>"Max is the reason this program is funded. If he walks, I cannot replace his expertise before the review. Learn to work around his temper."</blockquote>
<p>Her calendar is full of sponsor meetings. You understand what she fears losing, but she has made his reputation your responsibility. She promises no intervention. You leave without making a contemporaneous written record.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Return to the milestone work->Defect]]</div>

:: Record [consequence tone-support] {"position":"500,500"}
(set: $first to "record", $documented to true)
<div class="eyebrow">01 / A RECORD</div>
<h1>Facts you can stand behind</h1>
<p>You note the date, the chart correction, the words you remember, and who was in the room. You separate what you heard from what you inferred. You retain the relevant messages you are authorized to access in the company's approved workspace.</p>
<p>The note cannot make the room safer by itself. It can keep the sequence from dissolving into a general claim that you and Max simply do not get along.</p>
<p>You do not open Eli's private files or collect unrelated conversations. This is a record of your experience, not a dossier on your coworkers.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Return to the milestone work->Defect]]</div>

:: Quiet [consequence tone-caution] {"position":"800,500"}
(set: $first to "quiet")
<div class="eyebrow">01 / GETTING THROUGH THE WEEK</div>
<h1>Keep your head down</h1>
<p>You correct the chart and say nothing more. You calculate the rent due before your next paycheque. This choice buys a quieter afternoon, not assurance that it will never happen again.</p>
<p>You have not asked Jean for help or made a written record. When Eli offers to show you another test, you almost refuse: another question might expose another mistake.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Return to the milestone work->Defect]]</div>

:: Defect [decision stage-defect tone-caution] {"position":"500,680"}
<div class="eyebrow">02 / FORTY-EIGHT HOURS TO THE DEMO</div>
<h1>The bridge slips</h1>
(if: $first is "jean")[<p>Jean's refusal is still with you. Going through the manager has not made it easier to surface a problem.</p>](else-if: $documented)[<p>Your record is saved. You can distinguish the technical work from the way Max treated you, even if the lab will not.</p>](else:)[<p>You have kept your concern to yourself. No manager has heard it from you.</p>]
<p>A quick head turn sends the virtual bridge drifting across the table. You reproduce it twice. The failing path crosses Eli's timestamp conversion code, but you have not isolated the cause.</p>
<p>Max wants a clean rehearsal this afternoon. A hidden defect could embarrass the team; a public discussion could expose Eli to another tirade.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Ask Eli to review and test a fix together->Pair]]
[[Attempt a rushed repair alone->Solo]]
[[Raise the defect in the team review->Open]]</div>

:: Pair [consequence tone-support] {"position":"200,850"}
(set: $repair to "pair")
<div class="eyebrow">02 / SHARED REVIEW</div>
<h1>Two sets of eyes</h1>
<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"The conversion is mine, but the headset clock changed last week. Let's test the assumption before we blame a person."</blockquote>
<p>You trace both clocks, fix the boundary condition, and add a regression test. The additional checks move the rehearsal to the following morning. Max complains about the lost afternoon.</p>
<blockquote><b>Diane</b>"We can show the failure and the passing tests. We need both in the review."</blockquote>
<p>Eli leaves his notes open beside yours. For the first time, asking a question has made the room feel larger. The tested repair is ready for the revised rehearsal.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Read the manuscript draft->Credit]]</div>

:: Solo [consequence tone-risk] {"position":"500,850"}
(set: $repair to "solo")
<div class="eyebrow">02 / AN UNREVIEWED FIX</div>
<h1>The shortcut spreads</h1>
<p>You change the conversion without asking Eli. The original movement looks stable, but you have not checked the reset path. At rehearsal the headset reconnects, the tracker stalls, and the scene disappears.</p>
<blockquote><b>Max</b>"You broke the whole thing. Neither of you belongs on that stage."</blockquote>
<p>You own the inadequate review. Max owns the humiliation he directs at you and Eli.</p>
<p>The team rolls back your patch. Eli and another engineer reproduce the reset failure with you, then review the revised fix. The demonstration is delayed two days for regression tests. It will use that reviewed build, not your rushed patch.</p>
<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"Next time, ask me. Trying to keep me out of trouble left both of us guessing."</blockquote>
<div class="choices">[[Read the manuscript draft->Credit]]</div>

:: Open [consequence tone-caution] {"position":"800,850"}
(set: $repair to "open")
<div class="eyebrow">02 / A VISIBLE RISK</div>
<h1>Name the defect</h1>
<p>You show the failing test at the team review. Max turns from the trace to Eli.</p>
<blockquote><b>Max</b>"So this is what you call finished?"</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>Diane</b>"The failure is repeatable. Let's review the clock assumptions before assigning blame."</blockquote>
<p>Max talks over you. You did not cause his choice to humiliate Eli. The team now has a shared issue record, and an engineer chairs a focused technical review. The corrected build passes the expanded tests; rehearsal moves by a day.</p>
<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"The defect had to come out. I wish he could hear a problem without making someone the problem."</blockquote>
<div class="choices">[[Read the manuscript draft->Credit]]</div>

:: Credit [decision stage-credit tone-risk] {"position":"500,1030"}
<div class="eyebrow">03 / WHO GETS TO SIGN?</div>
<h1>The missing names</h1>
<p>The draft paper includes your calibration evaluation and Eli's tracking work. Both names have disappeared from the author list.</p>
(if: $repair is "solo")[<blockquote><b>Max</b>"After that rehearsal, neither of you has earned a place on this paper."</blockquote><p>The regression required correction. It did not erase the research you had already done.</p>](else:)[<blockquote><b>Max</b>"Authors deliver on my schedule. If you hold up the demo, you don't get to stand behind the result."</blockquote><p>The delay made the demonstration more reliable. Max is using credit to punish the people who made the risk visible.</p>]
<p>Jean is copied on the draft.</p>
<blockquote><b>Jean</b>"We cannot reopen every decision before the sponsor presentation. Send the slides."</blockquote>
<p>Eli quietly asks whether you noticed the list. You have time for one immediate response before the next workday.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Challenge the decision with contribution records->Challenge]]
[[Talk privately with Eli about support and consent->Support]]
[[Accept the decision for now to avoid another confrontation->Accept]]</div>

:: Challenge [consequence tone-caution] {"position":"200,1200"}
(set: $credit to "challenge", $challenged to true)
<div class="eyebrow">03 / CREDIT IS NOT A REWARD FOR OBEDIENCE</div>
<h1>A traceable objection</h1>
<p>You send Max and Jean the version history of your evaluation, its use in the paper, and the shared tracking records. You ask for a contribution-based authorship review for both of you. You cite work records you may access, not Eli's private views.</p>
<blockquote><b>Max</b>"You want to argue about names when we should be shipping?"</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>Diane</b>"I want the names to reflect the work."</blockquote>
<p>Jean acknowledges receipt but leaves the list unchanged pending discussion. Your objection and the contribution trail are now documented. This establishes an authorship dispute; it does not independently prove every earlier insult.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Consider what comes next->Debrief]]</div>

:: Support [consequence tone-support] {"position":"500,1200"}
(set: $credit to "support", $supported to true)
<div class="eyebrow">03 / ELI'S DECISION</div>
<h1>Ask before sharing</h1>
<blockquote><b>Diane</b>"I can describe what I saw. Is there anything you want to add yourself? I won't pass on this conversation without your permission."</blockquote>
(if: $repair is "pair")[<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"Working through the tests together helped. I wrote an account of the review and the credit decision. You may give that statement to Priya, with my name. Nothing else from this conversation."</blockquote><p>His permission is specific. You can carry that statement, or leave him to decide whether to send it himself.</p><div class="choices">(link: "Accept his permission to share that statement")[(set: $consent to true)(go-to: "Debrief")]
(link: "Keep the statement private; he can send it himself")[(set: $consent to false)(go-to: "Debrief")]</div>](else:)[<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"I want my credit back. But I can't risk a statement with my name on it right now. Please keep this conversation between us."</blockquote><p>You agree. He has not given permission to share his private account. That does not prevent you from reporting your own treatment or what you personally witnessed.</p><div class="choices">[[Respect his boundary and consider next steps->Debrief]]</div>]

:: Accept [consequence tone-caution] {"position":"800,1200"}
(set: $credit to "accept")
<div class="eyebrow">03 / AN IMMEDIATE COMPROMISE</div>
<h1>Send the slides</h1>
<p>You send the presentation and do not dispute the author list. You want a reference and another paycheque, and today you cannot face a fresh confrontation.</p>
<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"I thought those results were yours too."</blockquote>
<p>You say they are. He returns to his desk. The silence between you has a different weight now. Your work still exists in the repository, but there is no written authorship objection from you and no permission to share a private statement from Eli.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Consider what comes next->Debrief]]</div>

:: Debrief [scene] {"position":"500,1400"}
<div class="eyebrow">BEFORE THE NEXT DECISION / TAKE STOCK</div>
<h1>What you can carry</h1>
(if: $documented)[<p>You have a dated account of the first outburst. Its value is specificity, not a promise of a finding.</p>](else-if: $first is "jean")[<p>You can describe your conversation with Jean from memory, while making clear that you did not record it at the time.</p>](else:)[<p>You can describe the first outburst from memory. You have not previously told Jean about it.</p>]
(if: $challenged)[<p>Your written authorship objection links directly to the contribution history. Jean has not corrected the list.</p>](else-if: $supported)[<p>You listened to Eli without treating him as evidence to collect.</p>](else:)[<p>You have not challenged the credit decision. The list still excludes both of you.</p>]
(if: $consent)[<p>Eli has authorized sharing his named statement with Priya only. That permission is not permission to circulate it through the lab.</p>](else:)[<p>You have no permission to share a private statement from Eli. Your own observations remain yours to report.</p>]
<p>Priya, an HR adviser outside Jean's reporting line, has a slot for an options conversation. You decide to hear the process before choosing a longer-term response.</p>
<div class="choices">[[Hear Priya's options->Options]]</div>

:: Options [decision stage-future tone-caution] {"position":"500,1580"}
<div class="eyebrow">04 / THE LONGER VIEW</div>
<h1>No guaranteed ending</h1>
<blockquote><b>Priya</b>"This conversation isn't a formal complaint. If you file one, separate your experience, what you witnessed, and what others have authorized you to share. We may need to disclose relevant details to examine it fairly. I can't promise secrecy or a particular finding."</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>Diane</b>"And while that happens?"</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>Priya</b>"We can discuss temporary reporting arrangements and vacancies elsewhere. Report any retaliation. Neither a transfer nor a review makes the lab's problems disappear. You can also return to this process later."</blockquote>
<p>These are options at this fictional company. You have not yet filed a complaint. You weigh the opportunity, your well-being, and what you can change for the people still in the lab.</p>
<div class="choices">[[File a factual formal report->Report]]
[[Request a transfer and plan a safer exit->Exit]]
[[Stay and build safer peer practices->Peers]]
[[Keep working without further action->Silence]]</div>

:: Report [response tone-caution] {"position":"50,1780"}
<div class="eyebrow">04 / PUTTING AN ACCOUNT ON RECORD</div>
<h1>The scope of the report</h1>
<p>You report your own treatment, the events you witnessed, and the removal of earned credit. You distinguish recollection from records.</p>
(if: $documented)[<p>You attach the dated outburst note and relevant messages.</p>](else:)[<p>You label the outburst account as a later recollection, not a contemporaneous record.</p>]
(if: $challenged)[<p>You include the acknowledged authorship objection and contribution history.</p>](else:)[<p>You identify the shared work history for the reviewer to examine. You do not claim to have sent an earlier authorship objection.</p>]
(if: $consent)[<p>You give Priya only Eli's authorized statement. She contacts him directly about its scope before relying on it.</p>](else:)[<p>You include no private statement from Eli. Priya accepts your report without requiring him to participate.</p>]
<blockquote><b>Priya</b>"I'll arrange a reviewer outside this management chain. We will distinguish what we can establish from what remains unsettled."</blockquote>
(if: ($documented and $challenged) or $consent)[<div class="choices">[[Follow the review over the next six weeks->E1]]</div>](else:)[<div class="choices">[[Follow the review over the next six weeks->E2]]</div>]

:: Exit [response tone-support] {"position":"350,1780"}
<div class="eyebrow">04 / A BOUNDARY</div>
<h1>Leave the reporting line</h1>
<p>A testing vacancy in another group offers a transfer after a handover. It is less prestigious than this research post, but it keeps your salary. If the transfer falls through, you will search while employed instead of betting your rent on an immediate departure.</p>
<blockquote><b>Priya</b>"I can ask that the transfer be handled outside Jean's team. An exit account would record your concerns, but it would not automatically start the full review you declined today."</blockquote>
<p>You can leave a factual account of your own experience or focus on the handover. Neither option includes Eli's private account.</p>
<div class="choices">(link: "Leave a factual exit account and transfer")[(set: $exitAccount to true)(go-to: "E3")]
(link: "Transfer without an exit account")[(set: $exitAccount to false)(go-to: "E3")]</div>

:: Peers [response tone-support] {"position":"650,1780"}
<div class="eyebrow">04 / WORK WITHIN REACH</div>
<h1>A smaller circle of influence</h1>
<p>You propose two-person review, a shared defect log, and a contribution ledger before the next paper. You do not circulate private accounts of abuse.</p>
(if: $repair is "pair")[<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"We already know reviewing together helps. Let's make it normal instead of a favour."</blockquote>](else-if: $repair is "solo")[<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"I'll help if review is a requirement. We cannot keep repairing things in secret because we're afraid to ask."</blockquote>](else:)[<blockquote><b>Eli</b>"Keep the failures visible, but keep the review about the work. That's the rule I want."</blockquote>]
(if: $supported)[<p>Because you respected his boundary, Eli agrees to help draft the review checklist.</p>](else:)[<p>Eli agrees to try the checklist for one sprint. You will need to earn his confidence beyond a single meeting.</p>]
<p>Jean permits the trial because it may reduce missed deadlines. She declines to reconsider Max's authority.</p>
<div class="choices">[[See what changes after one month->E4]]</div>

:: Silence [response tone-risk] {"position":"950,1780"}
<div class="eyebrow">04 / THE NEXT MILESTONE</div>
<h1>Keep delivering</h1>
<p>You decide against a formal complaint, a transfer, or a peer initiative for now. The decision protects your immediate place on the project. It does not give Max permission to mistreat people.</p>
(if: $repair is "solo")[<p>The demo uses the reviewed replacement patch after the two-day delay. Your original regression is gone because the team tested and corrected it.</p>](else-if: $repair is "pair")[<p>The demo uses the fix you reviewed with Eli after the rehearsal moved by a morning.</p>](else:)[<p>The demo uses the tested fix from the public technical review after the one-day schedule change.</p>]
<div class="choices">[[Watch the sponsor presentation->E5]]</div>

:: E1 [ending outcome-good] {"position":"50,2030"}
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 1 OF 5 / ACCOUNTABILITY BEGINS</div>
<h1>A door opens slowly</h1>
(if: $consent)[<p>The reviewer checks Eli's authorized statement against the shared work history and your account. The accounts corroborate the use of humiliation and credit as pressure.</p>](else:)[<p>Your dated notes and acknowledged authorship objection let the reviewer trace the sequence. In a separate interview, Jean confirms she deferred your written authorship objection instead of addressing the use of credit as punishment. Eli has not supplied a private statement.</p>]
<p>The authorship review restores both earned credits. An experienced interim supervisor takes over daily reviews while Max's conduct and Jean's response are examined. You are not asked to replace Max.</p>
(if: $repair is "solo")[<p>The technical record still includes your rushed regression, its rollback, and the two-day correction. Accountability does not erase the work you needed to improve.</p>](else:)[<p>The tested repair remains part of the record: reliable work required review, not humiliation.</p>]
<p>The next research milestone moves while supervision changes. Some colleagues are relieved; others are guarded. A revised reporting process is promised, but you will judge it by whether people can use it.</p>
<div class="reflection"><h2>What this route asks</h2><p>Your specific account made scrutiny possible in this story; it was not a formula guaranteeing justice. ACM 1.5 supports recognizing actual contributions. Principles 3.3 and 3.4 connect leadership to working conditions and effective ethical processes. What would show that this change lasts after the reviewer leaves?</p></div>
<div class="choices">(link: "Restart with a fresh set of choices")[(restart:)]</div>

:: E2 [ending outcome-mixed] {"position":"250,2030"}
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 2 OF 5 / REVIEW UNRESOLVED</div>
<h1>An open file</h1>
<p>The reviewer can trace contributions but cannot yet settle all the accounts of Max's conduct. Interviews conflict, and some colleagues will not speak on the record. The paper's author list remains under review.</p>
(if: $documented)[<p>Your dated account gives the reviewer a clear starting point. Without an earlier authorship objection or an authorized corroborating statement, more inquiry is needed in this route.</p>](else-if: $challenged)[<p>Your written objection supports the credit dispute. It does not, by itself, establish everything that happened in earlier meetings.</p>](else:)[<p>Your recollection is part of the record. The reviewer still needs to compare it with other information.</p>]
<blockquote><b>Priya</b>"Unresolved does not mean false. We'll keep the review open. For now, your work will be reviewed by a supervisor outside Max's line."</blockquote>
<p>You keep your salary and gain some distance. You still do not know when, or whether, the remaining findings will arrive.</p>
(if: $repair is "solo")[<p>The demo has used the corrected, reviewed build after the two-day delay. That technical resolution has not resolved the workplace complaint.</p>](else:)[<p>The team's reviewed repair has stabilized the demo. A working prototype cannot settle how people were treated.</p>]
<div class="reflection"><h2>What this route asks</h2><p>ACM 1.2 supports reducing harm while uncertainty remains; 3.4 asks whether organizational processes make ethical commitments effective. Eli's silence does not disqualify your account. What support should be available before a final finding?</p></div>
<div class="choices">(link: "Restart with a fresh set of choices")[(restart:)]</div>

:: E3 [ending outcome-safe] {"position":"500,2030"}
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 3 OF 5 / A SAFER EXIT</div>
<h1>A different badge reader</h1>
<p>The transfer goes through after a two-week handover. You trade the famous lab for a testing team where questions are part of the job. The lost research opportunity hurts. So does realizing how much energy went into anticipating Max's mood.</p>
(if: $exitAccount)[<p>Your factual exit account remains with Priya. You requested no full investigation through that account, and none is promised.</p>](else:)[<p>You leave no exit account. The transfer documents a staffing change, not your reasons for wanting distance.</p>]
(if: $challenged)[<p>Your authorship objection is still pending. You retain the permitted contribution records and ask for a contact outside the lab to follow it up.</p>](else:)[<p>The old paper still omits your name. Leaving has not automatically restored earned credit.</p>]
(if: $supported)[<p>You tell Eli how to reach you. You keep his private conversation private in your new team.</p>](else:)[<p>You send Eli the technical handover. You do not assume he wants advice about leaving.</p>]
<p>Max still leads the old group. Protecting your well-being has not fixed its leadership.</p>
<div class="reflection"><h2>What this route asks</h2><p>ACM 1.2 makes reducing harm relevant to your own well-being too. Principle 3.3 places responsibility for working conditions on leadership. A boundary can be defensible even when others remain exposed. What responsibility can you carry without surrendering that boundary?</p></div>
<div class="choices">(link: "Restart with a fresh set of choices")[(restart:)]</div>

:: E4 [ending outcome-progress] {"position":"750,2030"}
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 4 OF 5 / LOCAL PROGRESS</div>
<h1>A better review table</h1>
<p>One month later, a second pair of eyes catches a reset error before rehearsal. The defect log records the assumption and fix, not an engineer's supposed worth.</p>
(if: $repair is "solo")[<p>The checklist includes the reset test missing from your rushed repair. Your mistake has become a useful lesson without becoming a licence to humiliate you.</p>](else:)[<p>The team has turned the reviewed repair into a repeatable practice rather than a one-off rescue.</p>]
(if: $challenged)[<p>The new contribution ledger supports your existing objection, but Jean has still not corrected the old manuscript.</p>](else:)[<p>The contribution ledger makes future work easier to trace. It does not correct the names on the old paper.</p>]
<p>Eli asks questions more readily in the peer sessions. When Max enters, the conversation still tightens. Jean calls the checklist a productivity improvement and avoids discussing why people were afraid to ask for help.</p>
<div class="reflection"><h2>What this route asks</h2><p>ACM 2.4 supports constructive professional review; 2.6 supports recognizing when you need help. You reduced technical and interpersonal risk within reach. Principles 3.3 and 3.4 expose the limit: peer care cannot substitute for accountable leadership. What would make these practices safe when Max objects?</p></div>
<div class="choices">(link: "Restart with a fresh set of choices")[(restart:)]</div>

:: E5 [ending outcome-cost] {"position":"1000,2030"}
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 5 OF 5 / SUCCESS WITH A COST</div>
<h1>The applause is real</h1>
<p>The bridge holds steady. The sponsor applauds. Funding continues, and so does your pay. Max presents the result as proof of his standards.</p>
(if: $repair is "solo")[<p>The applause comes two days later than planned, after rollback, peer review, and new tests. It does not validate the rushed patch or the tirade.</p>](else-if: $repair is "pair")[<p>Your shared review made this reliable demonstration possible. The presentation never mentions the morning it cost.</p>](else:)[<p>The public defect report and reviewed fix prevented a visible failure. Max takes credit for the corrected result.</p>]
(if: $challenged)[<p>Jean has acknowledged your authorship objection but has not acted on it. Leaving it unanswered has become another way to preserve the existing list.</p>](else-if: $supported)[<p>Eli thanks you for listening. His name, like yours, is still missing from the paper.</p>](else:)[<p>Your unchallenged omission becomes the circulated author list. Eli stops volunteering for presentation work.</p>]
<p>You edit tomorrow's question three times before sending it. A successful demonstration has not made this a safe place to learn.</p>
<div class="reflection"><h2>What this route asks</h2><p>Your need for stability was real, and Max remains responsible for his conduct. ACM 1.4 connects fairness to resisting abuse of power; 1.5 connects recognition to actual work. What does a team lose when people must choose between visible success and speaking honestly?</p></div>
<div class="choices">(link: "Restart with a fresh set of choices")[(restart:)]</div>

:: Frame [header] {"position":"1200,50"}
<div class="masthead"><span>THE PRICE OF PRESTIGE</span><span>GROUP 15 / AR LAB</span></div>
